traceability.evidence:
Implementation and tests for Story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md are present and passing.

Key implementation:
- src/index.ts defines the ESLint plugin entry point:
  - Exports a default `plugin` object with `rules` and `configs` (and `maintenance`) as expected for an ESLint plugin:
    ```ts
    /**
     * ESLint Traceability Plugin
     * @story docs/stories/001.0-DEV-PLUGIN-SETUP.story.md
     * @req REQ-PLUGIN-STRUCTURE - Provide foundational plugin export and registration
     * @req REQ-ERROR-HANDLING - Gracefully handles plugin loading errors and missing dependencies
     */
    const RULE_NAMES = [
      "require-story-annotation",
      "require-req-annotation",
      "require-branch-annotation",
      "valid-annotation-format",
      "valid-story-reference",
      "valid-req-reference",
      "prefer-implements-annotation",
      "require-test-traceability",
    ] as const;

    const rules: Record = {} as any;

    RULE_NAMES.forEach((name) => {
      try {
        const mod = require(`./rules/${name}`);
        rules[name] = mod.default ?? mod;
      } catch (error: any) {
        console.error(
          `[eslint-plugin-traceability] Failed to load rule "${name}": ${error.message}`,
        );
        rules[name] = {
          meta: { type: "problem", docs: { description: `Failed to load rule '${name}'` }, schema: [] },
          create(context) {
            return {
              Program(node: any) {
                context.report({
                  node,
                  message: `eslint-plugin-traceability: Error loading rule "${name}": ${error.message}`,
                });
              },
            };
          },
        } as Rule.RuleModule;
      }
    });

    const TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES = {
      "traceability/require-story-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/require-req-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/require-branch-annotation": "error",
      "traceability/valid-annotation-format": "warn",
      "traceability/valid-story-reference": "error",
      "traceability/valid-req-reference": "error",
      "traceability/require-test-traceability": "error",
    } as const;

    function createTraceabilityFlatConfig() {
      return { rules: { ...TRACEABILITY_RULE_SEVERITIES } };
    }

    const configs = {
      recommended: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
      strict: [createTraceabilityFlatConfig()],
    };

    const plugin = { rules, configs, maintenance };
    export default plugin;
    ```
  - Written in TypeScript; tsconfig.json configures CommonJS output and declaration files, matching `package.json` main/types (REQ-TYPESCRIPT, REQ-NPM-PACKAGE).
  - Dynamic rule loading via `RULE_NAMES` serves as a centralized rule registry (REQ-RULE-REGISTRY).

ESLint v9 flat-config integration:
- eslint.config.js is a flat-config array that conditionally loads the plugin (from ./src/index.js or ./lib/src/index.js) and registers it for JS/TS and specific test files:
  ```js
  const js = require("@eslint/js");
  let plugin;
  try { plugin = require("./src/index.js"); } catch (eSrc) {
    try { plugin = require("./lib/src/index.js"); } catch (eLib) { /* warn or throw in CI */ }
  }

  module.exports = [
    js.configs.recommended,
    { files: ["**/*.ts", "**/*.tsx"], plugins: { ...(plugin.rules ? { traceability: plugin } : {}) }, ... },
    { files: ["**/*.js", "**/*.jsx"], plugins: { ...(plugin.rules ? { traceability: plugin } : {}) }, ... },
    // test config & ignores
  ];
  ```
- tests/config/flat-config-presets-integration.test.ts uses `FlatESLint` from `eslint/use-at-your-own-risk` to validate that `configs.recommended` and `configs.strict` enable the plugin’s rules when used via the documented flat-config pattern (REQ-ESLINT-COMPAT):
  ```ts
  const config = [baseConfig, ...configs.recommended];
  const result = await lintTextWithConfig("function foo() {}", config);
  const ruleIds = result.messages.map((m) => m.ruleId).sort();
  expect(ruleIds).toContain("traceability/require-story-annotation");
  ```

